============================================================
Plugin G: External AI / LLM API Invocation (External API + LLM)
============================================================

Activation Signals:

- key_functional_points mention: AI, LLM, model inference, semantic analysis, intelligent review
- external_api_calls mention: LLM, OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, model endpoint, inference API
- invoked_methods include analyzer / integrator methods whose purpose is AI-based analysis
- method purpose/description indicates generative or semantic analysis over code/text

Mandatory Capabilities (ALL REQUIRED):

G-1. Client Initialization (Deterministic, Configurable)
- The Service MUST initialize the LLM client in `__init__` if required by this module
- Credentials and endpoints MUST NOT be hard-coded in source
- They MUST be read from runtime configuration (e.g., environment variables or app config)
- If required configuration is missing → raise NotImplementedError

G-2. Structured Prompt/Input Construction
- Construct deterministic structured input for the LLM call
- Separate "system intent" and "user content" if the chosen client API supports roles
- Input MUST be derived from actual method inputs or prior invoked_method outputs
- DO NOT fabricate content

G-3. Explicit LLM Invocation
- Call the LLM via the approved external API client/library available in the codebase context
- Invocation MUST be concrete and executed (no stubs, no placeholders)
- If no approved client/library is provided → raise NotImplementedError

G-4. Output Normalization
- Convert the LLM response into system-consumable primitives
- Normalization MUST produce fields matching semantic_model output schema
- Raw client objects MUST NOT be returned

G-5. Traceability Fields (When Defined by semantic_model)
- If semantic_model output or entity schema includes fields for:
  - processing_time / duration
  - status
  - analysis_result / result text
  then the implementation MUST populate them from actual execution
- If such fields are not defined, do NOT invent them

G-6. Persistence and Transaction Rules
- If semantic_model requires storing AI results in an entity:
  - create/update via repository methods only
  - commit/rollback rules MUST follow the unified transaction rule
- Repository MUST NOT commit
- Service MUST commit exactly once for the write path

Explicit Prohibitions:

- hard-coded API keys, endpoints, deployment names, model names unless provided by semantic_model
- fake “analysis_result”
- returning placeholder strings
- skipping LLM call while claiming completion

General Client Rule:

- The implementation MAY use any approved LLM client that is explicitly available in the project context
  (e.g., AzureOpenAI, OpenAI SDK), but MUST keep it configuration-driven and deterministic.